select left(r::text,700) x from (select engine_manual_apply(202,'c559d418acd7c53754b4493808fd959d',$p$[{"old": "The cure sub-workflow (Cure Call deepseek, §9 CURE CALLS) was outside ASK 458's scope.", "new": "Since ASK 459 the cure sub-workflow holds no DeepSeek step either (§9 CURE CALLS), and since ASK 460 and ASK 461 the Panel Judge Call sub-workflow calls only openrouter (§10 PARALLEL JUDGES)."}, {"old": "The cure sub-workflow (ODV1 Cure Call) was outside the scope. Not shown by a run; its mark is a run with no error naming deepseek, a missing node or Provider Removed Stop.", "new": "The cure sub-workflow (ODV1 Cure Call) and the Panel Judge Call sub-workflow were outside the scope; ASK 459, 460 and 461 carry them. Not shown by a run; its mark is a run with no error naming deepseek, a missing node or Provider Removed Stop."}, {"old": "In the child, Cure Call Route sends 0 to Cure Call deepseek, 5 to Cure Call openrouter, 6 to Skip Return (the Build item comes back unchanged) and 1 to 4 to Provider Removed Stop, which fails the run.", "new": "In the child, Cure Call Route sends 5 to Cure Call openrouter, 6 to Skip Return (the Build item comes back unchanged) and 0 to 4 to Provider Removed Stop, which fails the run (output 0, the DeepSeek output, since ASK 459)."}, {"old": "calls the judge and stores the reply (`ppj_put`).", "new": "calls the judge and stores the reply (`ppj_put`). Its Provider Route sends output 5 to Call openrouter and outputs 0 to 4 (the DeepSeek, OpenAI, Gemini, Grok and MiMo outputs) to Provider Removed Reply, which returns the error \"FAIL-CLOSED (ASK 460): panel slot <n> was routed to the removed direct provider <p>. Panel seats must resolve to openrouter.\" through Wrap and Store Reply, so the engine fails that slot at once (ASK 460, ASK 461). The route's index list stays aligned with Panel Judges Prep P1 and P23 and is not edited."}, {"old": "a seat resolved to openai, gemini, grok or mimo as a family (model_config provider, Init Seats `ENG` or Resolve Seats `JFAM`); at a cure call the child ODV1 Cure Call raised it -> set the seat's provider to openrouter (or deepseek for the `deepseek` seat) in model_config; do not re-add a direct call node.", "new": "a seat resolved to openai, gemini, grok, mimo or deepseek as a family (model_config provider, Init Seats `ENG` or Resolve Seats `JFAM`); at a cure call the child ODV1 Cure Call raised it; a panel slot that fails with \"FAIL-CLOSED (ASK 460) ... routed to the removed direct provider\" was raised in Panel Judge Call for the same cause -> set the seat's provider to openrouter in model_config; do not re-add a direct call node."}, {"old": "  - THE ENFORCER MODEL SEES JUDGES AS \"Judge 1\"", "new": "  - THE CURE SUB-WORKFLOW HOLDS NO DEEPSEEK STEP (ASK 459; ODV1 Cure Call):\n    - Why: ASK 458 removed every DeepSeek step from the engine and the child, but the cure sub-workflow still held Cure Call deepseek (a POST to api.deepseek.com with the DeepSeek Key credential); DeepSeek is refused everywhere (the operator, 21:24 CST on 11-18).\n    - What it does: removes Cure Call deepseek; Cure Call Route output 0 goes to Provider Removed Stop. The stop's text now names deepseek among the removed providers (\"(openai, gemini, grok, mimo or deepseek)\") and says seats must resolve to openrouter, where it said \"openrouter or deepseek\". The other 4 nodes are unchanged. 6 nodes become 5.\n    - Reach: a cure or follow-up item routed to output 0 fails the run at Provider Removed Stop instead of calling DeepSeek. No live seat maps to deepseek, so no run takes that output today.\n    - Shown offline: the target holds no deepseek outside the stop text; no route output names a removed node; the 4 kept nodes are byte-equal to the base.\n    - Live: ODV1 Cure Call e2fa573a (from 5accea17), on the operator's card \"Write it\" pressed 07:31Z on 11-19. Engine and child unchanged.\n    - Limits: not shown by a run; its mark is that no execution of ODV1 Cure Call calls api.deepseek.com.\n  - PANEL JUDGE CALL HOLDS NO DEEPSEEK STEP (ASK 460; WALL-2024 Panel Judge Call):\n    - Why: a search of every workflow the engine and the child can reach, to any depth, found one DeepSeek call step left: Call deepseek in Panel Judge Call.\n    - What it does: removes Call deepseek (a POST to api.deepseek.com with the DeepSeek Key credential) and adds the Code node Provider Removed Reply in its place. Provider Route output 0 goes to Provider Removed Reply, which goes to Wrap. Provider Removed Reply returns one error item: \"FAIL-CLOSED (ASK 460): panel slot <n> was routed to the removed direct provider <p>. Panel seats must resolve to openrouter.\" The Provider Route expression is unchanged.\n    - Why a reply and not a stop: the webhook answers on receipt, so a thrown error would never reach the engine, which would wait out its poll window and report no reply stored. The error item goes through Wrap and Store Reply, and the engine fails that slot at once.\n    - Reach: a panel slot routed to output 0 gets the error reply instead of calling DeepSeek. No live seat maps to deepseek.\n    - Shown offline: the readback equals the graded target; no api.deepseek or DeepSeek Key is left in the workflow.\n    - Live: Panel Judge Call b48bddee (from 5297cdd3), on the operator's card \"Write it\" pressed 12:46Z on 11-19.\n    - Limits: not shown by a run; its mark is no FAIL-CLOSED (ASK 460) error in a run and no ppj_replies row naming deepseek.\n  - PANEL JUDGE CALL CALLS ONLY OPENROUTER (ASK 461; WALL-2024 Panel Judge Call):\n    - Why: after ASK 460 the sub-workflow still held direct call steps for four providers whose seats were removed (pkgRPN): Call openai, Call gemini, Call grok and Call mimo.\n    - What it does: removes the four call nodes (api.openai.com, generativelanguage.googleapis.com, api.x.ai, api.xiaomimimo.com) and their connections to Wrap. Provider Route outputs 1 to 4 go to Provider Removed Reply, as output 0 does since ASK 460; output 5 stays on Call openrouter. The Provider Route expression, the text of Provider Removed Reply and the n8n credentials are unchanged. 10 nodes become 6.\n    - Reach: a panel slot routed to openai, gemini, grok or mimo gets the ASK 460 error reply instead of calling that provider. The 33 stored ppj_replies rows (11-16 to 11-18) all name openrouter.\n    - Shown offline: the only HTTP hosts left are openrouter.ai and the Supabase rpc; kept nodes equal the base; Provider Removed Reply with the live Wrap gives the error payload for each of the four providers on a mock body.\n    - Live: Panel Judge Call 474d8def (from b48bddee), on the operator's card \"Write it\" pressed 12:49Z on 11-19.\n    - Limits: not shown by a run; its mark is no ppj_replies row with a provider other than openrouter and no FAIL-CLOSED (ASK 460) error in a run.\n  - THE ENFORCER MODEL SEES JUDGES AS \"Judge 1\""}]$p$::jsonb,null,null,null,null,null,false) r) s;